            <ArticleTitle>Homozygous mutation in the NPHP3 gene causing foetal nephronophthisis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>818-820</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/nep.13097</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a foetal sonographic finding of hyper-echogenic kidneys, which led to a strategic series of genetic tests and identified a homozygous mutation (c.424C &gt; T, p. R142*) in the NPHP3 gene. Our study provides a rare presentation of NPHP3-related ciliopathy and adds to the mutation spectrum of the gene, being the first one from Pakistani population. With a thorough literature review, it also advocates for molecular assessment of ciliopathies to improve risk estimate for future pregnancies, and identify predisposed asymptomatic carriers.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 Asian Pacific Society of Nephrology.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
